WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.797
AND, OR, and NOT are the basic building blocks of SQL decision rules.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:10.152
AND means that every connected condition must be satisfied.

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:14.692
If a customer must be active and have a balance above a threshold,

00:00:14.692 --> 00:00:17.152
both conditions need to be true.

00:00:17.152 --> 00:00:21.212
OR means that at least one alternative can qualify.

00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:27.567
A student might need support if the student has a low exam score or has missed multiple assignments.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:32.537
Either condition is enough. NOT reverses a known condition.

00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:38.062
For example, we may want records that are active but not already completed.

00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:42.717
That sounds straightforward, but SQL adds one more truth state: UNKNOWN.

00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:47.632
This usually appears when a comparison involves NULL.

00:00:47.632 --> 00:00:51.832
It helps to think about these operators in terms of cohort size.

00:00:51.832 --> 00:00:57.537
AND usually makes a group smaller because each additional requirement removes rows.

00:00:57.537 --> 00:01:02.747
OR usually makes a group larger because more alternatives can qualify.

00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:07.782
NOT can exclude a group, but when the underlying expression is UNKNOWN,

00:01:07.782 --> 00:01:10.752
NOT does not magically turn it into TRUE.

00:01:10.752 --> 00:01:17.482
NOT UNKNOWN remains UNKNOWN. A useful real-world example is a loan-review rule.

00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:22.442
Suppose the rule requires income above a threshold and verified identity.

00:01:22.442 --> 00:01:28.607
If identity verification is missing, the system cannot honestly say the condition is true.

00:01:28.607 --> 00:01:31.747
It also may not be correct to say it is false.

00:01:31.747 --> 00:01:35.452
SQL represents that uncertainty as UNKNOWN.

00:01:35.452 --> 00:01:40.197
This is why Boolean logic in SQL is not only about syntax.

00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:44.268
It is about how certain or uncertain information affects decisions.
